  "executive_briefing": "As of late August 2026, the digital asset landscape is anchored by the impending September 15 Senate cloture vote on the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act (H.R. 3633), which serves as a pivotal catalyst for U.S. crypto market structure. While institutional Bitcoin ETF inflows have entered a Fatigue phase with stabilized treasury integration and minor net outflows in early 2026, regulatory certainty is reshaping developer architecture. A major structural shift is taking place between Ethereum's established EVM liquidity and emerging high-assurance, deterministic Bitcoin-native smart contract execution layers. Concurrently, cross-chain infrastructure is evolving rapidly from legacy wrapped bridges toward non-custodial atomic routing, enhancing liquidity interoperability between BTC and ETH.",
